      "message": "fix(xtask): the recording build writes its JSON to a file, not a pipe\n\nThe per-crate prebuild read cargo's JSON stdout through a pipe and joined\nthe reader after cargo exited. A descendant that outlives the build (the\nsccache server that the first rustc wrapper call starts) inherits that\nstdout, so the reader got no end of file until the server stopped. No\nwatchdog runs during that join. The JSON now goes to a temporary file;\nthe watchdog counts its size, and the gate reads it when cargo exits.\n\nPinned by watchdog_tests::a_recording_build_ends_when_cargo_exits_not_when_its_descendants_do\n(old code: 120 s wait, watchdog silent; new code: under 1 s).\n\nFixes #3675\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
